1
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:05,255
Bring them forward!

2
00:00:11,177 --> 00:00:12,429
Impressive…

3
00:00:12,512 --> 00:00:13,388
Peace?

4
00:00:29,529 --> 00:00:31,448
Why couldn't you protect him?

5
00:00:42,375 --> 00:00:44,627
Why couldn't you protect him?

6
00:00:52,093 --> 00:00:54,012
Why couldn't you protect him?

7
00:00:59,768 --> 00:01:01,269
Why?

8
00:01:02,103 --> 00:01:03,438
Why?

9
00:01:05,732 --> 00:01:07,650
Why won't you hit me back?

10
00:01:08,526 --> 00:01:10,153
Come on, hit me!

11
00:01:17,368 --> 00:01:19,746
Hit me back and tell me

12
00:01:21,289 --> 00:01:22,791
that Saizo's still alive!

13
00:01:23,958 --> 00:01:24,959
Come on!

14
00:01:25,668 --> 00:01:27,921
I said hit me!

15
00:01:28,463 --> 00:01:29,923
Hit me!

16
00:01:30,006 --> 00:01:31,508
Now we've lost Saizo, too.

17
00:01:33,468 --> 00:01:35,345
What are we supposed to do?

18
00:01:38,807 --> 00:01:41,392
If we go to war with the Tokugawa again…

19
00:01:42,143 --> 00:01:43,478
We've made peace.

20
00:01:44,145 --> 00:01:45,980
There's no need to worry about that.

21
00:01:47,649 --> 00:01:48,775
I'm not so sure.

22
00:01:50,485 --> 00:01:51,903
All we can do is pray.

23
00:02:05,375 --> 00:02:07,252
Does the peace treaty say

24
00:02:07,335 --> 00:02:09,838
the Tokugawa won't attack Osaka
once its defenses are down?

25
00:02:11,089 --> 00:02:12,423
How foolish.

26
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:15,301
Foolish, you say?

27
00:02:17,011 --> 00:02:17,929
Silence!

28
00:02:42,996 --> 00:02:43,997
Mother…

29
00:02:48,459 --> 00:02:50,336
Yukimura was right.

30
00:02:52,338 --> 00:02:54,966
Is this the end?

31
00:02:56,259 --> 00:02:57,093
Hideyori…

32
00:02:57,594 --> 00:02:58,678
If nothing else,

33
00:02:59,304 --> 00:03:02,557
you must live on.

34
00:03:06,144 --> 00:03:10,398
A flying half-demon
lurking deep in the south.

35
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:14,152
So it truly exists.

36
00:03:14,235 --> 00:03:15,069
There.

37
00:03:16,821 --> 00:03:19,782
Even Sanada is helpless
against attacks from above.

38
00:03:19,866 --> 00:03:22,994
I made this drug especially for you.

39
00:03:24,037 --> 00:03:25,705
Now drink.

40
00:03:26,581 --> 00:03:29,626
It will grant you even greater power.

41
00:03:33,296 --> 00:03:35,381
Offer me…

42
00:03:37,425 --> 00:03:39,761
a human sacrifice.

43
00:03:41,638 --> 00:03:44,807
Are you that eager to kill?

44
00:03:45,975 --> 00:03:47,560
Summon Imbeyama.

45
00:03:48,144 --> 00:03:48,978
Hanzo.

46
00:03:49,979 --> 00:03:50,813
Yes, my lord.

47
00:03:50,897 --> 00:03:53,733
Sanada will make his move again.

48
00:03:55,151 --> 00:03:58,613
He hasn't suffered nearly enough,

49
00:03:59,697 --> 00:04:00,782
but no matter.

50
00:04:02,659 --> 00:04:03,618
Kill him!

51
00:04:04,619 --> 00:04:05,954
It shall be done.

52
00:04:06,037 --> 00:04:08,414
Do not disappoint me again.

53
00:04:13,378 --> 00:04:16,714
Do you understand
the weight of your words?

54
00:04:17,507 --> 00:04:18,341
Yes.

55
00:04:19,133 --> 00:04:20,677
Fail again,

56
00:04:20,760 --> 00:04:23,388
and your lifelong ambition
will come to nothing.

57
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:26,349
Duty comes first.

58
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:30,144
Risk your life to fulfill your duty,

59
00:04:30,228 --> 00:04:34,565
and the Ogosho
will surely recognize your service.

60
00:04:44,075 --> 00:04:44,993
Hanzo.

61
00:04:47,078 --> 00:04:48,246
I've brought you

62
00:04:49,622 --> 00:04:54,002
a map of the Toyotomi
and Sanada troop positions.

63
00:04:54,836 --> 00:04:59,382
You betray your lord
without batting an eye?

64
00:05:00,550 --> 00:05:03,261
To die in service of one's lord
is one path.

65
00:05:03,970 --> 00:05:08,308
To read the changing tides
and serve another

66
00:05:09,267 --> 00:05:10,977
is just as valid.

67
00:05:12,145 --> 00:05:14,105
That's all there is to it.

68
00:05:31,581 --> 00:05:33,458
-Okuni.
-Yes, my lord.

69
00:05:34,208 --> 00:05:36,753
This is your final order.

70
00:05:38,046 --> 00:05:39,338
Kill Sanada

71
00:05:41,674 --> 00:05:43,009
before the war begins.

72
00:05:44,469 --> 00:05:45,470
Yes, my lord.

73
00:05:46,763 --> 00:05:48,514
SANADA DAISUKE
SANADA YUKIMURA

74
00:05:49,223 --> 00:05:50,558
What did you just say?

75
00:05:51,142 --> 00:05:54,103
I want Lord Hideyori to take the field

76
00:05:54,896 --> 00:05:56,856
as commander of the Toyotomi army.

77
00:05:58,232 --> 00:05:59,442
If he does,

78
00:06:00,359 --> 00:06:01,903
we still have a chance to win.

79
00:06:20,004 --> 00:06:21,631
Out of the question.

80
00:06:21,714 --> 00:06:23,341
I will not send Hideyori into battle.

81
00:06:23,424 --> 00:06:26,135
Have you seen the soldiers' faces?

82
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:29,847
It's as if they're looking
for a place to die.

83
00:06:30,389 --> 00:06:32,141
We've fallen right into
the Tokugawa's trap.

84
00:06:32,225 --> 00:06:36,521
Even Lord Urakusai,
who negotiated the peace, has disappeared.

85
00:06:36,604 --> 00:06:37,897
No wonder morale is low.

86
00:06:40,024 --> 00:06:46,697
But if Lord Hideyori takes the field,
he might reignite their fighting spirit.

87
00:06:46,781 --> 00:06:50,910
At the same time, the Tokugawa forces
will swarm to claim his head.

88
00:06:51,452 --> 00:06:54,413
Their ranks will break,
leaving their headquarters exposed.

89
00:06:54,497 --> 00:06:59,919
I'll seize that moment
and take Ieyasu's head with my ninja.

90
00:07:00,628 --> 00:07:01,796
A surprise attack?

91
00:07:01,879 --> 00:07:04,882
That could indeed turn the tide
in one fell swoop.

92
00:07:04,966 --> 00:07:07,426
But it's a double-edged sword.

93
00:07:07,510 --> 00:07:09,554
You won't escape unscathed.

94
00:07:09,637 --> 00:07:10,596
I know the risks.

95
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,014
But Hideyori…

96
00:07:12,098 --> 00:07:15,435
Shouldn't we put our faith
in Lord Yukimura?

97
00:07:16,227 --> 00:07:17,311
Harunaga!

98
00:07:17,395 --> 00:07:21,357
I don't wish to send Lord Hideyori
into battle either.

99
00:07:21,441 --> 00:07:22,900
-But--
-Do we…

100
00:07:24,527 --> 00:07:25,778
truly stand a chance

101
00:07:27,488 --> 00:07:28,948
if I take the field?

102
00:07:32,285 --> 00:07:33,244
Yes.

103
00:07:33,327 --> 00:07:34,370
Hideyori?

104
00:07:37,039 --> 00:07:37,915
Very well.

105
00:07:40,042 --> 00:07:41,502
I put my trust in you.

106
00:07:47,133 --> 00:07:48,968
Your resolve is admirable.

107
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:52,972
I understand your plan.

108
00:07:54,682 --> 00:07:57,226
Given all you've accomplished, Yukimura,

109
00:07:58,686 --> 00:08:00,980
I know I should trust you.

110
00:08:03,191 --> 00:08:04,192
But…

111
00:08:05,818 --> 00:08:07,862
I understand how you feel. However--

112
00:08:07,945 --> 00:08:09,238
No, you don't!

113
00:08:09,822 --> 00:08:11,157
You understand nothing.

114
00:08:15,870 --> 00:08:17,163
I'm afraid.

115
00:08:19,665 --> 00:08:22,210
I watched my ladies-in-waiting
die before my eyes.

116
00:08:25,546 --> 00:08:28,341
I don't want anyone else to die.

117
00:08:28,925 --> 00:08:29,842
In all likelihood,

118
00:08:30,510 --> 00:08:32,970
Ieyasu will launch
an all-out assault tomorrow.

119
00:08:33,971 --> 00:08:36,098
If we do nothing, we'll all perish here.

120
00:08:36,182 --> 00:08:38,309
No! That's not what I mean!

121
00:08:39,810 --> 00:08:41,145
Forget the strategy.

122
00:08:42,063 --> 00:08:43,272
I want to know…

123
00:08:45,149 --> 00:08:47,235
how you feel as his father.

124
00:08:50,446 --> 00:08:51,572
Hideyori is our son.

125
00:08:54,825 --> 00:08:57,370
Do you feel no hesitation at all

126
00:08:59,163 --> 00:09:00,331
about sending him

127
00:09:01,582 --> 00:09:03,000
into battle?

128
00:09:08,464 --> 00:09:09,757
None.

129
00:09:11,676 --> 00:09:13,135
It's for the Toyotomi clan.

130
00:09:13,219 --> 00:09:15,680
I don't understand!
I don't understand any of this…

131
00:09:17,473 --> 00:09:20,893
If you insist on taking
Hideyori into battle…

132
00:09:22,979 --> 00:09:24,272
then…

133
00:09:26,232 --> 00:09:27,692
kill me here and now!

134
00:09:37,326 --> 00:09:40,580
What's taking old man Yukimura so long?

135
00:09:41,205 --> 00:09:42,873
The Toyotomi aren't fools.

136
00:09:43,499 --> 00:09:48,129
They must know that sending Lord Hideyori
into battle is their only hope.

137
00:09:49,505 --> 00:09:50,923
Sorry to keep you waiting.

138
00:09:51,465 --> 00:09:53,342
Lord Hideyori's going into battle, right?

139
00:09:53,426 --> 00:09:55,094
What's our next move?

140
00:09:55,177 --> 00:09:57,096
Tell us your plan.

141
00:09:58,556 --> 00:09:59,890
What's in the box?

142
00:09:59,974 --> 00:10:03,936
Rewards for your victory
at the Sanadamaru.

143
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:06,147
They're yours.

144
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:09,108
Who cares about that now?

145
00:10:09,859 --> 00:10:13,029
This should be enough
to live on for a while.

146
00:10:13,779 --> 00:10:16,532
Lord Yukimura, don't tell me…

147
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:21,078
Lord Hideyori will not take the field.

148
00:10:22,997 --> 00:10:26,292
Our defenses are gone,
and we're vastly outnumbered.

149
00:10:27,251 --> 00:10:30,087
More and more ronin
are abandoning the Toyotomi.

150
00:10:30,671 --> 00:10:31,505
At this rate…

151
00:10:31,589 --> 00:10:35,051
Isn't that why we need
to get Lord Hideyori out there?

152
00:10:36,927 --> 00:10:38,262
Some of you

153
00:10:39,972 --> 00:10:42,016
have families waiting for you at home.

154
00:10:43,601 --> 00:10:45,519
Others have dreams of a life

155
00:10:46,812 --> 00:10:48,356
after this war.

156
00:10:49,899 --> 00:10:53,736
I'm the one who must bear
the burden of this defeat.

157
00:10:56,906 --> 00:10:59,367
I cannot drag you into this any further.

158
00:11:00,743 --> 00:11:01,911
Wait…

159
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:08,959
The Ten Braves are hereby disbanded.

160
00:11:12,755 --> 00:11:14,048
Hey, wait!

161
00:11:14,882 --> 00:11:16,300
You can't expect us to obey that.

162
00:11:16,384 --> 00:11:17,301
Sasuke!

163
00:11:17,385 --> 00:11:20,012
If you're going to give up this easily,
what was all of this for?

164
00:11:21,847 --> 00:11:24,350
I don't care whether Hideyori
takes the field or not.

165
00:11:25,267 --> 00:11:26,769
Saizo entrusted me

166
00:11:28,604 --> 00:11:29,772
with your life.

167
00:11:30,981 --> 00:11:32,483
He knew you'd keep fighting

168
00:11:32,566 --> 00:11:33,984
to the very end,

169
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:36,237
no matter what!

170
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:39,115
That's why…

171
00:11:41,409 --> 00:11:43,160
That's why he asked me to protect you!

172
00:11:46,789 --> 00:11:47,748
Hey.

173
00:11:48,457 --> 00:11:49,375
Hey, wait!

174
00:11:49,959 --> 00:11:50,835
Hey!

175
00:11:53,129 --> 00:11:54,588
Why isn't anyone stopping him?

176
00:11:55,256 --> 00:11:56,799
Are you going to let it end like this?

177
00:11:56,882 --> 00:11:59,510
Of course not!

178
00:12:01,846 --> 00:12:02,680
But…

179
00:12:05,266 --> 00:12:07,435
those are our lord's orders.

180
00:12:21,323 --> 00:12:22,658
Can I ask you something?

181
00:12:23,951 --> 00:12:28,080
Must a ninja always obey his lord?

182
00:12:29,874 --> 00:12:33,836
Even if he disagrees with the order?

183
00:12:35,212 --> 00:12:36,881
Yes. That's right.

184
00:12:46,307 --> 00:12:47,600
Damn it!

185
00:13:06,660 --> 00:13:08,370
Now this is nice!

186
00:13:08,454 --> 00:13:11,290
-Plenty of room to run a business, right?
-Yeah.

187
00:13:11,373 --> 00:13:13,876
With that reward,
we could each open our own shop.

188
00:13:15,336 --> 00:13:17,546
But neither place next door is available.

189
00:13:17,630 --> 00:13:19,590
You can open your restaurant here.

190
00:13:19,673 --> 00:13:21,050
No, no.

191
00:13:21,133 --> 00:13:23,385
We've only got each other.

192
00:13:23,969 --> 00:13:25,846
There's no way we're splitting up.

193
00:13:26,931 --> 00:13:28,224
Let's go see the next place.

194
00:13:35,272 --> 00:13:36,732
Are you all right?

195
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:40,569
Seikai…

196
00:13:40,653 --> 00:13:41,904
Don't tell me you're…

197
00:13:44,448 --> 00:13:45,658
From now on…

198
00:13:48,452 --> 00:13:50,329
live your own life.

199
00:13:57,711 --> 00:14:00,548
Why would you…

200
00:14:24,572 --> 00:14:25,573
Goodbye,

201
00:14:26,699 --> 00:14:27,658
Brother.

202
00:14:33,038 --> 00:14:33,998
Place your bets.

203
00:14:35,124 --> 00:14:36,500
Three and two. Odd.

204
00:14:40,546 --> 00:14:43,841
-All I needed was six coins.
-Coming in.

205
00:14:45,634 --> 00:14:46,760
Odd or even?

206
00:14:52,266 --> 00:14:54,310
-The bill, please.
-Of course.

207
00:14:55,686 --> 00:14:57,354
Is life hard?

208
00:14:58,439 --> 00:15:02,067
It's the same everywhere
ever since the Tokugawa took power.

209
00:15:08,866 --> 00:15:09,867
For the drinks.

210
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:13,746
I can't accept this much.
Why would you give me all this?

211
00:15:17,541 --> 00:15:18,876
Are you my father?

212
00:15:23,088 --> 00:15:24,089
I knew it.

213
00:15:44,777 --> 00:15:48,489
You're planning
to charge in alone, aren't you?

214
00:15:50,574 --> 00:15:51,617
Don't do it.

215
00:15:52,826 --> 00:15:54,912
What can you do on your own?

216
00:15:59,249 --> 00:16:02,169
I have a plan.

217
00:16:06,715 --> 00:16:07,967
If I make it back alive,

218
00:16:08,759 --> 00:16:10,260
there's something I want to tell you.

219
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:43,210
What do you think you're doing?

220
00:16:46,588 --> 00:16:48,048
You know…

221
00:16:50,092 --> 00:16:54,054
he always regretted giving me this scar.

222
00:16:57,099 --> 00:16:58,142
Ever since then,

223
00:17:00,102 --> 00:17:04,690
he told himself never to let
his feelings cloud his judgment.

224
00:17:08,277 --> 00:17:09,361
But then…

225
00:17:12,114 --> 00:17:13,782
you came along.

226
00:17:16,535 --> 00:17:18,704
And little by little, he changed.

227
00:17:23,959 --> 00:17:25,252
To spend

228
00:17:26,545 --> 00:17:28,005
my life with him…

229
00:17:29,965 --> 00:17:31,050
That's all…

230
00:17:38,098 --> 00:17:40,726
That's all I ever wanted.

231
00:17:46,148 --> 00:17:47,524
After all we've lost…

232
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:51,612
what are we even fighting for?

233
00:17:54,823 --> 00:17:56,950
No one can ever replace Saizo.

234
00:18:00,162 --> 00:18:01,330
But…

235
00:18:03,415 --> 00:18:05,084
I want to at least make sure…

236
00:18:08,128 --> 00:18:10,756
that he didn't die for nothing.

237
00:18:23,936 --> 00:18:27,314
Lord Sanada,
there's something I must ask you.

238
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:29,399
What is it, my lord?

239
00:18:31,401 --> 00:18:33,612
Why do you still fight alongside us?

240
00:18:35,823 --> 00:18:37,241
Out of loyalty to the Taiko?

241
00:18:39,076 --> 00:18:40,160
Or is it…

242
00:18:42,412 --> 00:18:43,789
out of a father's love?

243
00:18:46,333 --> 00:18:47,251
I simply

244
00:18:49,086 --> 00:18:51,130
wish to know how you feel.

245
00:18:57,970 --> 00:19:01,306
Why do we fight?

246
00:19:03,267 --> 00:19:04,643
For money?

247
00:19:06,603 --> 00:19:09,314
To leave our names in history?

248
00:19:11,150 --> 00:19:12,234
No.

249
00:19:12,901 --> 00:19:16,738
We fight for the peace of this land.

250
00:19:18,407 --> 00:19:21,785
This battle will end
our long years of war.

251
00:19:22,995 --> 00:19:27,583
The Toyotomi have
no strength left to resist.

252
00:19:29,042 --> 00:19:33,714
For the peace of everyone in this land,

253
00:19:34,673 --> 00:19:37,092
we launch an all-out assault tomorrow!

254
00:19:38,635 --> 00:19:39,761
One day.

255
00:19:40,679 --> 00:19:43,891
Take Osaka Castle in a single day!

256
00:19:43,974 --> 00:19:45,309
Yes, my lord!

257
00:19:58,155 --> 00:19:59,281
Is someone there?

258
00:20:15,964 --> 00:20:17,216
Do you really think

259
00:20:18,342 --> 00:20:20,510
you can take Ieyasu's head alone?

260
00:20:28,477 --> 00:20:31,563
So you've mastered
the art of disguise, Sasuke.

261
00:20:32,856 --> 00:20:34,358
Like I'd need…

262
00:20:35,859 --> 00:20:37,152
What are you talking about?

263
00:20:37,236 --> 00:20:39,446
If you want to fool me, lose that habit.

264
00:20:40,948 --> 00:20:43,992
Damn. Saizo left this behind.

265
00:20:44,076 --> 00:20:45,661
Not bad, huh?

266
00:20:49,331 --> 00:20:52,668
So you overheard my conversation
with Lord Matabe.

267
00:20:56,004 --> 00:20:57,923
Charging in alone without a plan?

268
00:20:59,132 --> 00:21:01,218
That's not the kind of gamble you'd make.

269
00:21:02,511 --> 00:21:06,390
I have no other choice.

270
00:21:09,184 --> 00:21:10,435
I'm saying

271
00:21:11,728 --> 00:21:13,272
I'm coming with you.

272
00:21:15,941 --> 00:21:18,193
I thought you served me for money,

273
00:21:19,444 --> 00:21:20,696
not out of loyalty.

274
00:21:23,156 --> 00:21:24,658
But my body…

275
00:21:26,410 --> 00:21:27,494
is itching to go.

276
00:21:28,161 --> 00:21:29,997
It keeps telling me to push on.

277
00:21:37,421 --> 00:21:40,549
Mind if we join you in that gamble?

278
00:21:56,815 --> 00:21:57,733
You all…

279
00:21:58,442 --> 00:22:01,403
We heard what you've
resolved to do, Father.

280
00:22:02,070 --> 00:22:03,697
We're fighting, too.

281
00:22:04,406 --> 00:22:08,201
I've never had much faith in myself.

282
00:22:09,619 --> 00:22:10,996
But with everyone here,

283
00:22:11,997 --> 00:22:14,207
maybe we can achieve the impossible.

284
00:22:15,334 --> 00:22:16,585
What are our chances?

285
00:22:16,668 --> 00:22:19,504
I'd say the odds are 99% against us.

286
00:22:19,588 --> 00:22:21,048
One percent's plenty.

287
00:22:23,383 --> 00:22:26,595
What's the point of gambling
if you don't bet on the long shot?

288
00:22:26,678 --> 00:22:30,557
You gambled away all your money,
so you need to earn some back, right?

289
00:22:30,640 --> 00:22:32,017
Shut up, will you?

290
00:22:33,018 --> 00:22:34,436
Shakespeare once said,

291
00:22:35,103 --> 00:22:39,608
"To be or not to be,
that is the question."

292
00:22:40,734 --> 00:22:41,693
But…

293
00:22:42,903 --> 00:22:48,325
it seems Sanada's ninja
care more about how they live.

294
00:22:53,038 --> 00:22:54,623
Where are Isa and old man Mochizuki?

295
00:22:54,706 --> 00:22:57,584
-Brother won't be coming.
-Neither will Mochizuki.

296
00:22:58,835 --> 00:23:00,754
They'd never disobey Father's orders.

297
00:23:03,006 --> 00:23:06,510
Now's your chance to leave.
The odds are against us.

298
00:23:06,593 --> 00:23:07,719
Even so…

299
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:13,391
For our fallen comrades.

300
00:23:16,812 --> 00:23:18,105
For loyalty.

301
00:23:22,484 --> 00:23:23,693
I'm putting…

302
00:23:26,113 --> 00:23:27,280
my faith in you.

303
00:23:45,423 --> 00:23:46,299
Very well.

304
00:23:47,551 --> 00:23:50,804
I'll give you our final plan now.

305
00:23:53,098 --> 00:23:56,226
I thank you all
from the bottom of my heart

306
00:23:56,935 --> 00:23:58,436
for defying my orders.

307
00:24:07,028 --> 00:24:08,655
I won't tell you to come back alive.

308
00:24:09,322 --> 00:24:12,409
But never choose a path you'll regret.

309
00:24:13,577 --> 00:24:17,080
Let these words guide you in battle.

310
00:24:18,665 --> 00:24:21,251
That is my final order.

311
00:24:22,544 --> 00:24:23,920
Is this…

312
00:24:30,886 --> 00:24:33,346
What will Sanada do tomorrow?

313
00:24:34,514 --> 00:24:37,100
He plans to attack our headquarters alone.

314
00:24:39,686 --> 00:24:40,770
Is that all?

315
00:24:45,525 --> 00:24:46,526
I can hear it.

316
00:24:47,819 --> 00:24:50,447
Your heart is racing.

317
00:24:52,365 --> 00:24:53,617
What have you learned?

318
00:24:57,787 --> 00:24:59,372
Forgive me for asking,

319
00:25:00,999 --> 00:25:02,209
but Lord Hanzo,

320
00:25:03,168 --> 00:25:05,921
have you never questioned an order?

321
00:25:11,259 --> 00:25:12,594
Tell me everything.

322
00:26:03,812 --> 00:26:04,771
Now…

323
00:26:05,563 --> 00:26:07,357
it's all yours to command.

324
00:26:08,525 --> 00:26:09,651
Just in time.

325
00:26:34,467 --> 00:26:36,594
Everything is ready.

326
00:26:38,054 --> 00:26:43,059
This will surely be
the last battle of my life.

327
00:26:44,894 --> 00:26:46,021
By sunset,

328
00:26:47,022 --> 00:26:50,358
the Ogosho will be a god to this nation.

329
00:26:58,158 --> 00:27:02,662
THE SUMMER SIEGE OF OSAKA

330
00:27:05,457 --> 00:27:06,458
Here it is.

331
00:27:08,543 --> 00:27:09,753
Are you certain?

332
00:27:09,836 --> 00:27:11,171
I've made my decision.

333
00:27:12,881 --> 00:27:16,134
I'll fight beside you to the end, Father.

334
00:27:17,886 --> 00:27:20,638
Let us pray for each other's victory.

335
00:27:23,475 --> 00:27:24,392
Yes, Father.

336
00:27:24,476 --> 00:27:25,560
Lord Yukimura!

337
00:27:25,643 --> 00:27:26,895
What is it?

338
00:27:45,121 --> 00:27:47,499
There's only one enemy! Don't panic!

339
00:27:48,249 --> 00:27:50,335
He's come to crush
our soldiers' morale again!

340
00:27:50,418 --> 00:27:51,878
We must hold him off,

341
00:27:52,420 --> 00:27:54,756
or the castle will fall
before we can take Ieyasu's head.

342
00:27:59,094 --> 00:28:00,011
Damn it.

343
00:28:06,893 --> 00:28:07,769
Damn it!

344
00:28:10,105 --> 00:28:11,731
Leave the bird to the monkey.

345
00:28:18,863 --> 00:28:19,781
Is that…

346
00:28:28,373 --> 00:28:29,666
Mochizuki…

347
00:28:29,749 --> 00:28:30,625
Old man!

348
00:28:30,708 --> 00:28:34,838
I've returned against your orders!

349
00:28:36,381 --> 00:28:38,633
Forgive me.

350
00:28:46,641 --> 00:28:48,143
Unno…

351
00:28:48,226 --> 00:28:49,102
UNNO ROKURO

352
00:28:49,185 --> 00:28:50,353
Lend me your strength.

353
00:29:10,248 --> 00:29:12,000
Curved Shot, Wild God!

354
00:29:29,893 --> 00:29:31,853
Nice shot, old man Mochizuki!

355
00:29:35,148 --> 00:29:36,399
Come on,

356
00:29:37,150 --> 00:29:38,276
you damn bird!

357
00:29:38,359 --> 00:29:39,861
Monkey!

358
00:29:41,321 --> 00:29:42,822
Don't take him head-on!

359
00:29:42,906 --> 00:29:44,616
His body's packed with explosives!

360
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:46,409
We've got no choice.

361
00:29:54,959 --> 00:29:56,127
Sasuke.

362
00:29:56,211 --> 00:29:58,087
That recklessness of yours

363
00:29:58,171 --> 00:30:00,632
reminds me of Unno in his youth.

364
00:30:02,383 --> 00:30:03,885
Take care of our lord.

365
00:30:08,056 --> 00:30:09,307
Old man…

366
00:30:18,358 --> 00:30:19,317
Mochizuki!

367
00:30:20,109 --> 00:30:21,361
Mochizuki!

368
00:30:25,448 --> 00:30:26,866
Magamaru!

369
00:30:26,950 --> 00:30:29,661
Ready!

370
00:30:29,744 --> 00:30:31,454
Begin!

371
00:30:32,288 --> 00:30:33,498
Here they come.

372
00:30:34,624 --> 00:30:35,667
Let's go.

373
00:30:36,209 --> 00:30:37,961
Don't let Mochizuki's death be in vain.

374
00:30:44,509 --> 00:30:46,886
Don't let Lord Mochizuki's death
be in vain!

375
00:30:53,768 --> 00:30:55,562
Follow me!

376
00:30:57,981 --> 00:30:59,357
Don't fall behind!

377
00:31:00,024 --> 00:31:02,068
Our army will take the castle.

378
00:31:03,611 --> 00:31:05,405
Attack!

379
00:31:27,343 --> 00:31:28,678
There are so many of them.

380
00:31:29,554 --> 00:31:31,431
There he is! It's Sanada Yukimura!

381
00:31:31,514 --> 00:31:33,016
-They found us!
-It's Sanada!

382
00:31:33,099 --> 00:31:36,603
Guess they won't let us
take Ieyasu's head so easily.

383
00:31:39,731 --> 00:31:41,316
Damn it! They just keep coming!

384
00:31:53,161 --> 00:31:54,662
Lord Hideyori…

385
00:31:58,416 --> 00:32:01,044
-It's Lord Hideyori!
-Lord Hideyori is here!

386
00:32:01,127 --> 00:32:02,754
Lord Hideyori has arrived!

387
00:32:02,837 --> 00:32:04,297
Fear nothing!

388
00:32:04,380 --> 00:32:06,424
Stand and fight!

389
00:32:07,675 --> 00:32:09,177
Hideyori's on the battlefield?

390
00:32:10,053 --> 00:32:12,680
Lord Hideyori is over there.

391
00:32:16,059 --> 00:32:17,101
Then…

392
00:32:18,353 --> 00:32:19,395
who's that?

393
00:32:21,064 --> 00:32:22,023
It can't be…

394
00:32:22,607 --> 00:32:23,942
My lord, a report!

395
00:32:24,609 --> 00:32:27,820
Enemy commander Toyotomi Hideyori
has taken the field!

396
00:32:27,904 --> 00:32:30,365
The Toyotomi forces are pushing us back!

397
00:32:30,448 --> 00:32:33,534
Damn it! What are you fools doing?

398
00:32:33,618 --> 00:32:34,911
In that case…

399
00:32:43,628 --> 00:32:46,464
The enemy troops
are converging on the battlefield.

400
00:32:46,547 --> 00:32:47,882
That must be Lord Daisuke.

401
00:32:48,758 --> 00:32:50,927
Thanks to him, there are fewer enemies.

402
00:32:51,844 --> 00:32:52,720
Seikai!

403
00:32:53,680 --> 00:32:54,722
I'm fine.

404
00:32:57,141 --> 00:32:58,017
Up ahead…

405
00:32:58,643 --> 00:33:00,728
Yes. Ieyasu's headquarters.

406
00:33:06,567 --> 00:33:07,527
That's…

407
00:33:08,361 --> 00:33:09,946
Too bad.

408
00:33:10,947 --> 00:33:13,616
We know all about your little plan.

409
00:33:15,368 --> 00:33:17,620
They're advancing as we speak!

410
00:33:17,704 --> 00:33:19,455
Enough! Get out!

411
00:33:26,921 --> 00:33:28,131
That's…

412
00:33:28,214 --> 00:33:29,882
The drug they used to enhance Tsuge.

413
00:33:32,093 --> 00:33:34,721
They don't have long to live.

414
00:33:35,680 --> 00:33:36,597
But…

415
00:33:39,726 --> 00:33:42,687
a little time is all we need.

416
00:33:51,529 --> 00:33:52,572
Hold this position.

417
00:34:14,302 --> 00:34:15,803
You're…

418
00:34:17,013 --> 00:34:19,223
Got time to stand there gawking?

419
00:34:19,307 --> 00:34:21,350
Where's the real Sanada?

420
00:34:22,018 --> 00:34:23,561
Like hell I'd tell you.

421
00:34:34,489 --> 00:34:35,823
Save your strength.

422
00:34:35,907 --> 00:34:38,201
Your fight isn't here.

423
00:34:57,887 --> 00:34:59,597
Seikai, you're incredible!

424
00:35:57,864 --> 00:35:58,865
Brother…

425
00:35:58,948 --> 00:35:59,991
Are you all right?

426
00:36:00,992 --> 00:36:01,993
You fool.

427
00:36:17,550 --> 00:36:19,677
Iron Hammer, Whirlwind!

428
00:37:10,853 --> 00:37:12,730
What incredible strength…

429
00:37:23,824 --> 00:37:24,659
Wait.

430
00:37:38,172 --> 00:37:39,507
Seikai…

431
00:37:41,676 --> 00:37:42,969
Seikai!

432
00:37:49,267 --> 00:37:50,184
Seikai…

433
00:37:54,063 --> 00:37:55,106
Seikai?

434
00:37:57,191 --> 00:37:58,776
-Isa!
-Seikai…

435
00:37:58,859 --> 00:38:00,444
Your eyes…

436
00:38:03,322 --> 00:38:04,490
Seikai…

437
00:38:14,000 --> 00:38:14,959
Sasuke…

438
00:38:16,377 --> 00:38:17,461
How's Seikai?

439
00:38:25,761 --> 00:38:26,971
He's fine.

440
00:38:29,557 --> 00:38:30,516
He's alive.

441
00:38:31,684 --> 00:38:33,102
He's still fighting.

442
00:38:34,812 --> 00:38:36,605
Seikai's strong!

443
00:38:38,274 --> 00:38:39,900
He's your brother, all right.

444
00:38:41,944 --> 00:38:43,237
Thank goodness…

445
00:38:52,580 --> 00:38:53,748
Seikai…

446
00:38:57,209 --> 00:38:58,711
I don't want to be alone.

447
00:39:03,632 --> 00:39:05,801
Let's open a restaurant together.

448
00:39:07,887 --> 00:39:10,181
I'm sure you'll get better, too.

449
00:39:11,015 --> 00:39:12,600
You'll be well again soon…

450
00:39:15,394 --> 00:39:17,229
Let's live out our lives…

451
00:39:20,399 --> 00:39:21,317
together…

452
00:39:23,903 --> 00:39:25,071
You can.

453
00:39:28,824 --> 00:39:30,034
Together,

454
00:39:31,952 --> 00:39:32,912
you can…

455
00:40:05,194 --> 00:40:06,278
Let's go.

456
00:40:20,418 --> 00:40:23,754
Wow, you really took a beating.

457
00:40:23,838 --> 00:40:25,631
Who the hell are you?

458
00:40:33,222 --> 00:40:36,517
Found you.

459
00:40:38,727 --> 00:40:40,062
That's strange.

460
00:40:40,146 --> 00:40:40,980
What?

461
00:40:41,063 --> 00:40:42,690
Why hasn't Hanzo shown himself?

462
00:40:50,865 --> 00:40:52,616
So you were here after all.

463
00:40:53,451 --> 00:40:54,994
Hattori Hanzo.

464
00:40:56,120 --> 00:40:58,873
You sent your men ahead
to clear a path to our headquarters,

465
00:40:59,874 --> 00:41:02,168
then followed behind them.

466
00:41:03,169 --> 00:41:04,712
What a cowardly tactic.

467
00:41:05,880 --> 00:41:08,424
So you knew our plan all along.

468
00:41:10,259 --> 00:41:11,469
What's so funny?

469
00:41:13,554 --> 00:41:14,638
Two fours.

470
00:41:15,431 --> 00:41:17,349
Looks like death awaits us both.

471
00:41:18,642 --> 00:41:20,102
You're…

472
00:41:20,186 --> 00:41:21,896
Master of a hundred ninja arts,

473
00:41:23,230 --> 00:41:25,232
Nezu Jinpachi.

474
00:41:25,858 --> 00:41:28,903
That damn Okuni tricked me.

475
00:41:45,085 --> 00:41:47,213
I'll tell you…

476
00:41:49,673 --> 00:41:53,886
what Lord Yukimura's…

477
00:41:56,263 --> 00:41:58,015
real orders were.

478
00:42:00,142 --> 00:42:05,523
FOLLOW YOUR HEART
YUKIMURA

479
00:42:13,197 --> 00:42:15,533
You'd never understand.

480
00:42:16,784 --> 00:42:19,745
The greatest gamble of all…

481
00:42:26,252 --> 00:42:28,796
is putting your faith in someone.

482
00:42:31,465 --> 00:42:32,716
Flame Release!

483
00:42:37,304 --> 00:42:38,639
There's smoke…

484
00:42:40,641 --> 00:42:41,892
Don't look back!

485
00:42:43,644 --> 00:42:46,397
Don't let Nezu's sacrifice be in vain.

486
00:42:48,274 --> 00:42:49,441
Let's go.

487
00:42:57,199 --> 00:42:58,200
Go!

488
00:43:01,453 --> 00:43:03,539
There it is. The enemy headquarters.

489
00:43:03,622 --> 00:43:05,958
Enemy attack! Enemy attack!

490
00:43:06,041 --> 00:43:07,835
Sanada is here!

491
00:43:22,558 --> 00:43:23,517
Ieyasu!

492
00:43:24,518 --> 00:43:25,561
Yukimura.

493
00:43:26,645 --> 00:43:29,106
I never thought you'd make it this far.

494
00:43:29,773 --> 00:43:31,859
I must commend you, even as my enemy.

495
00:43:33,736 --> 00:43:37,406
But can your blade reach me?

496
00:43:59,720 --> 00:44:00,638
Sasuke!

497
00:44:00,721 --> 00:44:01,930
You're alive.

498
00:44:02,014 --> 00:44:03,349
Of course I am.

499
00:44:04,183 --> 00:44:06,185
Leave the small fry to us!

500
00:44:14,193 --> 00:44:15,319
Wait.

501
00:44:17,321 --> 00:44:18,614
Finish him, old man!

502
00:44:20,741 --> 00:44:23,786
Put an end to this goddamn age!

503
00:44:24,328 --> 00:44:25,162
Wait!

504
00:44:40,844 --> 00:44:42,763
We did it! Hell yeah!

505
00:44:44,181 --> 00:44:45,182
Not yet.

506
00:44:48,102 --> 00:44:49,812
This man isn't Ieyasu.

507
00:44:50,854 --> 00:44:51,980
What do you mean?

508
00:44:52,689 --> 00:44:53,524
A body double.

509
00:44:54,525 --> 00:44:55,609
No way.

510
00:45:01,407 --> 00:45:04,034
Sanada has reached our headquarters.

511
00:45:04,618 --> 00:45:06,245
Good thing we took precautions.

512
00:45:06,328 --> 00:45:07,538
Indeed.

513
00:45:07,621 --> 00:45:11,333
I wonder what
Sanada's face looks like now.

514
00:45:14,253 --> 00:45:16,463
True despair comes

515
00:45:17,506 --> 00:45:19,383
when hope is snatched away.

516
00:45:31,770 --> 00:45:33,730
After all we've done,

517
00:45:33,814 --> 00:45:35,357
we still can't reach him?

518
00:45:36,358 --> 00:45:37,317
Let's find him.

519
00:45:37,901 --> 00:45:39,653
He couldn't have gotten far.

520
00:45:40,320 --> 00:45:41,363
Yes, my lord.

521
00:45:41,447 --> 00:45:43,073
Ieyasu…

522
00:45:43,824 --> 00:45:45,451
I'll kill that bastard.

523
00:45:46,368 --> 00:45:48,704
Still as hotheaded as ever, I see.

524
00:45:54,918 --> 00:45:55,836
Saizo?

525
00:45:56,962 --> 00:45:59,756
You're alive?

526
00:46:12,644 --> 00:46:13,562
Why…

527
00:46:13,645 --> 00:46:15,898
Subtitle translation by: Sayo Takada

528
00:46:15,981 --> 00:46:17,858
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION

